# Markdown: prettier has NO authority here, so make that explicit (#3947).
#
# `format:check` is `prettier --check 'src/**/*.ts' 'tests/**/*.ts'
# 'scripts/**/*.ts'` — it checks ZERO markdown. So running `prettier --write`
# on a .md file is all risk and no benefit: nothing verifies the result, and
# prettier rewrites the WHOLE file rather than the part you edited. Measured
# on origin/main, 2026-08-01:
#   docs/ci-policy.md   5 +/6 -  — and one of those is CONTENT DAMAGE, not
#                                  restyling: a backtick span adjacent to
#                                  **bold** makes prettier mis-parse the
#                                  emphasis run and DELETE the spaces between
#                                  words (`src/**`stays both-lane` —`target:).
#                                  Third occurrence of this mangling, second
#                                  file (cf. 7327b3ac).
#   README.md          17 +/12 -  (tables realigned, *em* -> _em_ in prose)
#   ROADMAP.md         18 +/16 -  (same)
#   CLAUDE.md           1 +/1 -   — also CONTENT DAMAGE: it de-indents the
#                                  continuation line of a list item ("404
#                                  Branch not / protected") to column 0,
#                                  which drops the following fenced code
#                                  block out of the list item.
# Ignoring them turns `prettier --write <doc>` into a no-op instead of a
# silent rewrite, which closes the class without asking anyone to remember
# which files are gated.
#
# CLAUDE.md is INCLUDED in this ignore, and that does NOT make the #3947
# sync-vs-prettier agreement vacuous. The agreement is asserted by
# tests/issue-3947.test.ts, which calls prettier's PROGRAMMATIC `format()` on
# the generated block in a temp fixture — and `format()` does not consult
# .prettierignore. That test is the stronger detector anyway: it isolates the
# anchor block from unrelated CLAUDE.md prose drift (which is exactly what
# started confounding the manual `prettier --write CLAUDE.md` check), and it
# runs in CI on every PR rather than when someone remembers.
**/*.md
